1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,740
Ruben Santana, the chef and owner of Bark BBQ in Brooklyn, New York, takes his barbecue very, very seriously.

2
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,339
We came hungry and he said no problem.

3
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:10,960
He broke out his Texas-style smoked brisket.

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,189
First up, three slices of lean brisket.

5
00:00:13,919 --> 00:00:15,419
Then the brisket burn ends.

6
00:00:16,079 --> 00:00:17,640
Nice crispy work.

7
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:20,079
Which he is very proud of and he should be.

8
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,000
And a couple slices of fatty brisket.

9
00:00:23,269 --> 00:00:27,559
Next, their longaniza smoked sausage, which you can get sliced or whole.

10
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:30,579
A nice ball of his juicy pulled pork.

11
00:00:31,679 --> 00:00:33,539
His beautifully glazed pork ribs.

12
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:35,560
I mean, look at those.

13
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,820
He also serves up chicharron.

14
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:44,719
Gives it a squeeze and serves it with limes.

15
00:00:45,359 --> 00:00:47,280
He showed us his brand new menu item.

16
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:55,500
Smoked brisket carnitas on top of fried plantains with cilantro, avocado sauce, pickled onions and cilantro.

17
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,759
His smoked and fried chicken.

